From: Reuben Olinsky <reubeno@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dnf: skip Flatpak side payload when Flatpak GI typelib is missing

The DNF payload module unconditionally tells PayloadsService that it
needs a Flatpak "side payload" (for flatpak-preinstall(...) Provides
support).  PayloadsService.activate_payload() then constructs that side
payload, which imports pyanaconda.modules.payloads.payload.flatpak.
flatpak_manager.  That module performs

    gi.require_version("Flatpak", "1.0")
    from gi.repository.Flatpak import ...

at module top level.  When the Flatpak-1.0 GObject-Introspection typelib
(shipped by flatpak-libs) is not present, gi.require_version() raises
ValueError("Namespace Flatpak not available"), which Anaconda then
re-raises as

    pyanaconda.modules.common.errors.general.AnacondaError:
        Namespace Flatpak not available

This makes flatpak / flatpak-libs an effectively hard runtime
dependency of every DNF-based Anaconda install, even when the user has
no flatpak-preinstall(...) Provides in their package set.

Make the Flatpak preinstall support optional by probing the GI typelib
in DNFModule.needs_flatpak_side_payload().  When it is unavailable we
return False, which prevents PayloadsService from creating the side
payload and avoids importing any of the Flatpak-using modules.

All other consumers of side_payload already guard with
``if self.side_payload`` / ``if self.active_payload.side_payload``, so
no further changes are required.

This change is a no-op when flatpak-libs is installed.
---
 pyanaconda/modules/payloads/payload/dnf/dnf.py | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pyanaconda/modules/payloads/payload/dnf/dnf.py b/pyanaconda/modules/payloads/payload/dnf/dnf.py
--- a/pyanaconda/modules/payloads/payload/dnf/dnf.py
+++ b/pyanaconda/modules/payloads/payload/dnf/dnf.py
@@ -397,7 +397,16 @@ class DNFModule(PayloadBase):
         return required_space.get_bytes()
 
     def needs_flatpak_side_payload(self):
-        return True
+        """Does this payload need an extra payload for Flatpak installation."""
+        try:
+            import gi
+            gi.require_version("Flatpak", "1.0")
+            from gi.repository import Flatpak  # noqa: F401
+        except (ImportError, ValueError):
+            log.info("Flatpak GI typelib not available, "
+                     "skipping Flatpak side payload.")
+            return False
+        return True
 
     def get_flatpak_refs(self):
         """Get the list of Flatpak refs to install.
